  "text_md": "# ARTICLE IN PRESS\n\n![](<0678963a20825044fed5401fedb69bc7a3e54de6_page_2_processed_images/imageFile1.png>)\n\nELSEVIER\n\nMidwifery xxx (xxxx)\n\nContents lists available at ScienceDirect\n\n# Midwifery\n\njournal homepage: www.elsevier.com/locate/midw\n\n![](<0678963a20825044fed5401fedb69bc7a3e54de6_page_2_processed_images/imageFile2.png>)\n\nMidwifery\n\nCorrigendum\n\nCorrigendum to “ Midwifery continuity of carer in an area of high socioeconomic disadvantage in London: A retrospective analysis of Albany Midwifery Practice outcomes using routine data (1997 – 2009) ” [Midwifery 48 (2017) 1 – 10]\n\nCaroline S.E. Homer, RM, MMed(ClinEpi), PhD Professor a , ⁎ , Nicky Leap, DMid Adjunct Professor of Midwifery a , Nadine Edwards, PhD Independent Researcher a , b , c , Jane Sandall, PhD, CBE Professor, NIHR Senior Investigator b , c\n\na Centre for Midwifery, Child and Family Health, Faculty of Health, University of Technology Sydney, PO Box 123, Broadway, Sydney, New South Wales 2007, Australia b Division of Women's Health, Faculty of Life Sciences & Medicine, King's College London, United Kingdom\n\nDivision of Women's Health, Faculty of Life Sciences &  Medicine, King's College London, United Kingdom\n\nWomen's Health Academic Centre, St. Thomas' Hospital, London SEI 7EH, United Kingdom\n\nThe authors regret that on page 8 we inadvertently referred to NICE as providing policy and policy direction. This was incorrect. NICE provides national clinical guidance based on systematic reviews. The sentence should read: A large study comparing perinatal outcomes by planned place of birth (Birthplace in England Collaborative Group, 2011) supported the clinical guidance to o ﬀ er women with low risk pregnancies a choice of birth settings, including birth at home (NICE, 2014). The authors would like to apologise for any inconvenience caused.\n\nThe authors would like to apologise for any inconvenience caused.\n\nDOI of original article: http://dx.doi.org/10.1016/j.midw.2017.02.009 ⁎ Corresponding author.\n\nCorresponding author.\n\nE-mail address: caroline @uts edu.au (CSE. Homer). homer(\n\nhttp://dx.doi.org/10.1016/j.midw.2017.05.013\n\n0266-6138/ © 2017 The Author(s). Published by Elsevier Ltd. This is an open access article under the CC BY-NC-ND license (http://creativecommons.org/licenses/BY-NC-ND/4.0/).\n\n",
